# The repository is authored with LF endings everywhere, and two things break
# when a checkout rewrites them: bash scripts stop running, and the provider
# spec staleness check reads CRLF yaml against LF built json and calls it
# stale, which failed continuous integration on the Windows runner only.
# One rule ends both: every text file is LF, in the index and in the working
# tree, on every platform. Git detects binary files on its own under text=auto.
* text=auto eol=lf
